Pico RISC-V: ChangeLog

What changed, day by day, newest first: one line per commit (its short
hash and subject; `git show <hash>` has the whole story). Every line of
code was written by Claude (Anthropic), in Claude Code; @padcom directed.

2026-10-18  Speed

	* The SDL window (macOS): no Window menu, so the keys of macOS's
	          window commands (F11: Fill) are the guest's
	* 00685f7 The page: the function keys are the screen's wherever the
	          focus is (but the terminal), and in full screen, the keyboard
	          lock's
	* 5da8c09 JIT: atomics (AMOs but MIN/MAX, LR, SC) compiled, and reading
	          sstatus or setting or clearing its SIE
	* fa49d60 JIT: jumps to a block further on in the page go straight to
	          its code, not through the switch (Debian's boot 3% faster)
	* 6c58de1 JIT: MULH* and FENCE compiled, CSR instructions (but satp) go
	          on in compiled code, and jumps back to a page's own function
	          go through its switch, not a call (Debian's boot 4% faster)

2026-10-15  Doom: a sound card, Freedoom, a day of fixes, Debian only, and a name: Pico RISC-V

	* Packages: @padcom/pico-risc-v-hart (the core, a computer for bare-metal
	          programs: run(), a pluggable UART, a C runtime, an example) and
	          @padcom/pico-risc-v-relay (npx); one pointer on the screen.
	* README.md, ChangeLog: the project is Pico RISC-V; how it came to be.
	* cefee91 Debian only: Alpine is gone, and the static site (GitHub Pages)
	          boots Debian
	* 3339f99 Alpine: the keyboard's map from X's start (setxkbmap), so Doom's
	          arrow keys work
	* 831f857 Alpine: Fluxbox instead of twm, so that full screen works
	          (Doom's Alt+Enter)
	* aa9e147 Sound: each message goes back 50 ms before it has played (the
	          last once it has)
	* ad88182 Alpine: bash, for freedoom1 and freedoom2 (and the menu's
	          Freedoom)
	* 3f7f97d Debian: Doom without OpenGL's window
	          (SDL_FRAMEBUFFER_ACCELERATION=0)
	* eb3bbc5 Sound: a virtio sound card, heard in the page and the CLI's
	          window; Freedoom on both distributions

2026-10-14  Windows: VNC, an SDL window, a page-fitted screen, a resizable virtio GPU

	* 6604d61 JIT: a memory group whose check failed checks again after its
	          first access
	* 77446ec JIT: pages are compiled after 8000 instructions, not 2000
	* 0bab7be The screen follows the window: a virtio GPU whose display
	          resizes
	* 520743e JIT: loads and stores off one value share one translation check
	* a187823 The page: the screen by default, fitted to it, a terminal a
	          click away
	* 97a5dc8 npm start --display: the screen in a window of its own (SDL)
	* ce92286 VNC: macOS's Screen Sharing gets in (RFB 3.3 asks for a
	          password)
	* 4d9b5e1 npm start --display: the screen, through VNC

2026-10-13  A face: more JIT, a framebuffer, a keyboard and a mouse, desktops

	* 6ccad21 Desktops on the screen: Xfce on Debian, X with twm on Alpine
	* 0b9bc82 A keyboard and a mouse for the screen (virtio input)
	* 80445f9 A screen: a framebuffer in RAM, shown in the page (?display)
	* 276150e JIT: the harts share compiled code
	* 65675d0 JIT: a block that loops to itself is compiled as a loop
	* 61b683b SMP: the hart threads handle the CLINT themselves

2026-10-12  Speed and the browser: a JIT, multicore on threads, Debian in a web page, a static site

	* 6389467 JIT: code runs on into the next block, and blocks run whole
	          (2.8× faster)
	* 83deb53 The page keeps its disk: changes saved in the browser, across
	          reloads
	* c8e318f A network for the static site: npm run relay, on this machine
	* 5185338 Terminal size: a virtio console, which tells Linux the size and
	          changes
	* fc8a093 Alpine Linux, and the emulator as a static web site (GitHub
	          Pages)
	* 54190dd In a web browser: npm run web (Debian boots in the page, on 4
	          harts)
	* 6c917e8 SMP: each hart on a thread of its own (4 harts: parallel work
	          3.3× faster)
	* d5daddb SMP: machines with several harts (Debian boots on 4)
	* 44d7cc4 Terminal: interrupts, so Linux's console isn't polled (1.3 →
	          ~500 KB/s)
	* 1bcf44b JIT: compiled pages go on in each other's code (Debian boot
	          about 5% faster)
	* ca30f4f JIT: hot pages compiled to WebAssembly (Debian boot 43 → 28 s)
	* 7687d4a Port forwarding into the guest: ssh -p 2222 root@localhost
	* 6decc2c Trim Debian's boot: 60 → 43 s to the login prompt (benchmark)
	* 10036f2 Faster blocks; tests and benchmarks boot a pristine Debian disk

2026-10-11  A real machine: MMU, virtio disk and network, the core in Rust/WebAssembly, RV64GC, Debian

	* 3dd3d42 Decoded-instruction cache: run() executes whole decoded basic
	          blocks
	* f709d80 Debian from its cloud image: Debian's OpenSBI, U-Boot, GRUB and
	          kernel
	* e135a0f Debian only, RV64 only: removed the 32-bit and nommu Linux
	          images and RV32
	* 5dbcf84 Added setup scripts for macOS and Linux: clone, set up, npm run
	          start:debian
	* e9c01eb Added a Debian 13 (riscv64) disk: systemd, networking and apt on
	          the RV64 machine
	* 03a49fd Implemented floating point (F and D): the CPU is now RV32GC /
	          RV64GC
	* 20e7e88 Implemented RV64 and Sv39, and added a 64-bit Linux image
	* 6d9f1e0 Implemented compressed instructions (RV32C) and rebuilt the
	          Linux image with them
	* 89895ff Ported the interpreter to Rust to gain 5x speed improvement
	* 5aee736 Implemented virtio-net based networking and storage outside of
	          ramfs using ext4
	* 47143b9 Implemented MMU and MC

2026-10-10  A small start: an RV32 interpreter in TypeScript, booting a tiny Linux without an MMU

	* 264c41f Added option to close the Linux session after logging out
	          (Ctrl+D)
	* 4f7d01a Added option to compile the linux from scratch
	* 6c5c32a Initial import
